{
  "requirement": "For each token category, `reported` sums the provider’s measurements and `missing_attempts` counts attempts that supplied no measurement for that category. A reported zero is a measurement. Input and output totals count each token once, even when the provider also reports it in a cache or reasoning breakdown.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct TokenCount {\n    pub reported: u64,\n    pub missing_attempts: u64,\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for TokenCount;\nimpl Copy for TokenCount;\nimpl Debug for TokenCount;\nimpl Default for TokenCount;\nimpl Serialize for TokenCount;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The two marked tests cover each obligation of `requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.TokenCount`. Both are in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs`.\n\n- **`reported` sums per category.** `cache_retains_usage_across_validators_and_sums_each_token_category` runs two measured attempts across two validators that share one cache. It asserts reported totals of 19 input, 13 output, 5 cached, 3 cache-creation and 8 reasoning tokens. A mis-summed or cross-wired category would fail.\n- **`missing_attempts` counts attempts with no measurement.** The same test has one throttled attempt with no usage, and it asserts `missing_attempts == 1` for every category. `validators_keep_measured_tokens_after_failed_attempts_and_evidence_reuse` has three attempts, and only one reports usage. It asserts input and output missing counts of 2, and it asserts cache-creation missing is 3 because that attempt omits the category. A partially measured attempt is therefore distinguished from a fully unmeasured one.\n- **A reported zero is a measurement.** The second test supplies `reasoning_tokens(0)` and asserts `reported == 0` with `missing_attempts == 2`. That is 3 attempts minus the zero-reporting one, so the zero was not counted as missing.\n- **Input and output count each token once.** Both tests supply cached and reasoning breakdowns alongside the totals. Inputs 12 and 7 with cached 3 and 2 must total 19, and outputs 9 and 4 with reasoning 5 and 3 must total 13. A single run with input 120 and cached 20 must report input 120. Adding the breakdown into the total would fail these assertions.\n- **Struct shape and trait impls.**\n  - `Clone`, `Copy`, `Debug`, `Default` and `Serialize` come from one plain `#[derive]` on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs#struct[TokenCount]`. `#[non_exhaustive]` is a declaration with no behavior. These derives have no conditional and no transformation of their own, so they are exempt from a dedicated test.\n  - The tests also exercise `Copy` and `Default` indirectly. They copy `TokenCount` values out of arrays, and a fresh validator's usage is asserted as all zeros.\n\nI found no unacknowledged gap and no marking gap.",
